  "content": {
    "title": "Wendy's offering free Frosty and fries today. How to get 'dunk deal'",
    "text": "Updated April 7, 2026, 12:32 p.m. ETThe Michigan Wolverines aren't the only winners this March Madness.Wendy's lovers can score a free Frosty and fries with no purchase required April 7, in celebration of the NCAA championship game.Americans have Michigan basketball player Roddy Gayle Jr. to thank for the freebies. The first dunk during the men's national championship game unlocked the offer. And Gayle Jr. made it happen.Here's how to get the dunk deal.Wendy's free Frosty and fries dunk promotionThe promotion includes a free small fry and a free small chocolate or vanilla Frosty. The offer is available in-restaurant only at participating locations during all lunch and dinner hours. No purchase is necessary to get the deal.Wendy's near me. How to find nearest Wendy's location in CincinnatiFor a list of Wendy's locations in and around Cincinnati, see here. If you live outside of the Cincinnati area, you can use the restaurant's locator to find your nearest Wendy's location.What time does Wendy's open?Wendy's hours vary by location. Most Wendy's in Cincinnati open at 6 a.m. or 6:30 a.m. Some don't open until 10 a.m. Others are open for 24 hours. Check your nearest location for its hours.What time does Wendy's start serving lunch?Typically, Wendy’s serves its lunch and dinner menu from 10:30 a.m. to midnight, though some locations differ.What time does Wendy's close?Wendy's hours vary by location. Most Wendy's in Cincinnati close at midnight or 1 a.m. Some locations are open until 2 a.m. or 3 a.m. Others are open for 24 hours. Check your nearest location for its hours.",
